          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Cordelia\",\"addressee\":\"Lear\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Unhappy that I am, I cannot heave\\nMy heart into my mouth: I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you, Your Majesty.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Cordelia directly presents her love for Lear as a true present emotional and relational state. Its deliberate restraint does not reduce its clear avowal force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.87,\"reason\":\"The focal avowal is immediately qualified as love owed under Cordelia's existing filial bond. It therefore moderately invokes an established relational obligation—Cordelia's duty as Lear's daughter to love him—rather than making a new or unlimited promise. Her subsequent explanation identifies related duties of obedience and honour.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Return those duties back as are right fit,\\nObey you, love you, and most honour you.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The expression is a controlled, propositionally explicit avowal, carefully limited by Cordelia's account of her bond. It is not represented as a reflex-like affective outburst or expressive discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Unhappy that I am, I cannot heave\\nMy heart into my mouth: I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":1,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.78,\"reason\":\"Beyond avowing love and invoking filial obligation, the restrained expression weakly functions as resistance to Lear's demand for a competitive, reward-seeking declaration. Cordelia answers the question but declines the hyperbolic performance sought by the love test.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"what can you say to draw\\nA third more opulent than your sisters? Speak.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Nothing will come of nothing: speak again.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love your majesty\\nAccording to my bond; no more nor less.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"In a public court proceeding, Lear asks his daughters to declare how much they love him while linking their answers to shares of his kingdom. After initially answering “Nothing,” Cordelia gives the marked restrained avowal, addressing Lear both as her father and sovereign. Lear rejects the answer as inadequate and warns that it may damage her fortunes.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Cordelia invokes, rather than newly creates, her existing filial bond: she presents herself as owing Lear the fitting love and duties of a daughter, later naming obedience, love, and honour. She expressly limits this to “no more nor less” than that bond requires. Lear does not accept the formulation as an adequate response to his test and asks her to amend it. The focal expression does not promise exclusive love or an unlimited future commitment.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages are recognisable as William Shakespeare's King Lear, including the opening love test and the later reconciliation and final scene.\",\"limitations\":\"The dramatic language clearly establishes avowal and invocation of filial duty, while the later supplied passages strongly support genuine affection through Cordelia's concern, attempted restoration, and grief for Lear. Nevertheless, the precise inward state at the original moment cannot be established independently of the represented words and actions, and the focal expression itself does not specify detailed future conduct or formal terms of commitment.\"}"
        }
